    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n65299" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μᾰχ-ητής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οῦ</span>,
			ὁ, 
			Aeol.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μαχαίτας</span></b> 
		<i><span class="en">
			Alc.
			33
		</span></i>; 
			Dor.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μαχᾱτάς</span></b> 
		<i><span class="en">
			Pi.
			<u>N.</u>
			2.13
		</span></i>, etc.; 
			Lacon.
		
		<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μαχᾱτάρ </span></b> ( <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μᾰχ-άταρ</span></b>  cod.) <i><span class="en">
			Hsch.
		</span></i>: (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μάχη</span>):—<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>fighter, warrior</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μικρὸς μὲν ἔην δέμας ἀλλὰ μ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					5.801
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">θείειν ταχὺς ἠδὲ μ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Od.
					3.112
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Τρῶάς φασι μ. ἔμμεναι ἄνδρας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					18.261
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φὼς μ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pi.
					<u>N.</u>
				</span></i>
			 l. c.: as Adj., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μαχατὰν
				θυμὸν αἰσχυνθῆμεν</span> his <i>warrior</i> heart,
				ib.<i><span class="en">
				9.26
			</span></i>: in later Prose, <i><span class="en">
				LXX
				<u>Jo.</u>
				6.3
			</span></i>,al.</div>
